+# Incidents brief, August–September 2026
+
+Action status per the 30 September on-call sync.
+
+## 11 August 2026: ingest stall, full disk
+
+- **Impact:** Incoming data stalled about 2.5 hours overnight; customers saw stale dashboards. No data lost.
+- **Cause:** A malformed batch jammed ingest in endless retries; their logs filled the database disk until it refused writes.
+- **Fix:** Restarted ingest with the bad batch set aside; cleaned the database without blocking writes; compressed old logs.
+- **Actions:**
+  - 80% disk alert: Sunil, done.
+  - Stop bad batches jamming ingest: Jonas, open (in review).
+  - Faster paging escalation (no owner named): done; Elif configured 15-minute escalation.
+
+## 21 September 2026: expired API certificate
+
+- **Impact:** For 47 minutes the public API refused secure connections; nearly all customers and browsers failed.
+- **Cause:** The certificate expired; automatic renewal had failed silently all month on an outdated access token.
+- **Fix:** Renewed the certificate and restarted the API; renewal now uses the current token and alerts on failure.
+- **Actions:**
+  - Reminder 14 days before expiry: Priya, done.
+  - Days-to-expiry alert: Priya, open.
+  - Expiry check in weekly checklist: Tomasz, open.
+  - Responders record steps during incidents: Mara, done (on-call handover notes).
